# Chroma library, modern Earth: bold ways, batch 4 (stage A). Each first bold way has its links (well and badly; well only
# for moments only for those under 18), and each link carries its own bold way. Second bold ways have no links.

# ================================================================ a breakthrough in your work

== bold: a breakthrough in your work / R
base: tell everyone you know tonight, without checking a thing
likelier_if: has [savings] +10; mark 'took a wild risk' +5
- R | drop every evening and weekend for the find, and follow it wherever it leads | v: stimulation, self-direction | act: drop every evening and weekend for the find and follow it wherever it leads | chance: 40 | grants: patron | drops_if_fails: kind:community
works: A backer hears of the find, comes to see it work, and offers to pay {Ns} way for as long as it takes.
works: {N} works on it day and night, and a backer who believes in it takes on the bills from then on.
fails: The find will not come right again, and the club {N} stopped going to has given {Ns} place to someone else.
fails: By spring the find has stalled, and the group {N} belonged to for years has quietly let {N} go.

== the backer wants an answer
tier: link
of_bold: a breakthrough in your work / R
side: well
delay: 1-2
holds: patron
stages: juvenile+
age: 15-92
stakes: .7
tone: mixed
life: work, money
horizon: months
roles: rival, mentor
earth: your backer has paid for a year of your work, and now a rival has a cheaper copy on sale
scene: For a year the backer has paid {Ns} way while the find grew. Now {rival} has a cheaper copy in the shops, and the backer wants to know what {N} means to do about it.
scene gone: {rival} has moved on, but the cheap copy is still in every shop, and the backer wants to know what {N} means to do about it.
- W | ask the judges of the trade to rule on whose work it was | v: conformity, universalism | chance: 70
- U | make the find better than the copy, and let the work speak for itself | v: self-direction, achievement | chance: 72
- B | cut the price below the copy's, and win the shops back | v: power, achievement | chance: 68
- R | go round to the rival's door and have it out face to face | v: stimulation | chance: 66
- G | keep making it the slow, careful way, for the people who already trust it | v: tradition, security | chance: 75
works: The backer stays, and the work goes on into a second year.
works: The people who use the find stay loyal, and the copy fades from the shops.
fails: The backer's patience thins, and every meeting is about money now.
fails: The copy sells better than anyone expected, and {N} loses a season to it.

== bold: the backer wants an answer / B
base: cut the price below the copy's, and win the shops back
likelier_if: has [striking a deal] +10; has [selling] +5
- B | go into business with the backer, and take the find to market yourselves | v: achievement, power | act: go into business with the backer and take the find to market together | chance: 45 | requires: patron | grants: business partner | takes_if_fails: patron
works: {N} and the backer shake on a firm of their own, and the find goes out under both their names.
works: The backer becomes {Ns} partner in the business, and together they beat the copy within the year.
fails: The talk of shares turns sour, and the backer takes the money elsewhere for good.
fails: The backer will not be a partner, and pulls out of the find altogether by summer.

== back at the bench
tier: link
of_bold: a breakthrough in your work / R
side: badly
delay: 1-2
stages: juvenile+
age: 15-92
stakes: .6
tone: mixed
life: work, meaning
horizon: months
roles: colleague, mentor
earth: the find fell through and your old place at the club went with it, and now an old colleague says there is a bench free
scene: Since the find fell through, {N} has kept {Ns} head down, and the old crowd at the club has moved on without {N}. {colleague} rings: there is a bench free in a workshop across town, if {N} wants to try again.
scene gone: {colleague} has moved away, but the message is still on the phone: a bench free in a workshop across town, if {N} wants to try again.
- W | keep to steady work first, and save up before you try again | v: security, conformity | act: keep to steady work first and save up before trying again | chance: 78
- U | go back through the old notes, and find where it went wrong | v: self-direction | chance: 75
- B | sell the old notes to a firm that can afford to finish the work | v: power, achievement | chance: 70
- R | take the bench tomorrow, and start again from nothing | v: stimulation | chance: 68
- G | let it rest for now, and go back to work that feeds the family | v: security, tradition | chance: 80
works: Slowly {N} finds a way to work again, and the find stops feeling like a wound.
works: The new work goes well enough, and the old notes are kept safe in a drawer.
fails: Money is tight, and {N} wonders whether it was all a mistake.
fails: Nothing seems to move for months, and the old notes gather dust.

== bold: back at the bench / U
base: go back through the old notes, and find where it went wrong
likelier_if: has [fixing things] +10; has [lab work] +5
- U | rent the bench with your last savings, and rebuild the find step by careful step | v: self-direction, achievement | act: rent the bench with their last savings and rebuild the find step by step | chance: 40 | requires: savings | grants: workshop | takes_if_fails: savings
works: Step by step it comes right, and the rented bench becomes a workshop of {Ns} own.
works: {N} finds the old mistake in the third month, and keeps the workshop on for good.
fails: The rent eats the last of the savings, and the find still will not hold.
fails: By winter the savings are gone, and the bench goes to someone else.

== bold: a breakthrough in your work / B
base: keep it secret until you have worked out how to profit from it
likelier_if: has [striking a deal] +10; has [contact in the trade] +5
- B | borrow all the bank will lend, make the find yourself, and sell it shop by shop | v: achievement, power | act: borrow all the bank will lend, make the find themselves and sell it shop by shop | chance: 30 | grants: selling | title_if_fails: bankruptcy or insolvency in their history
works: {N} talks shop after shop into taking the find, and from then on can sell almost anything to almost anyone.
works: The first run sells out in a month, and {N} has found a knack for selling that never leaves.
fails: A bigger firm brings out something like it first, the loans cannot be paid, and {N} goes through a formal insolvency.
fails: The shops will not take it, the debts come due, and {N} is declared insolvent before the year is out.

# ================================================================ a new job at last

== bold: a new job at last / G
base: go back to the line of work you know, close to home, for good
likelier_if: has [old family name] +10; has [contact in the trade] +5
- G | turn down the city money for the lower pay at your family's old yard | v: tradition, security | act: turn down the city money for the lower pay at their family's old yard | chance: 45 | grants: crew that has your back | takes_if_fails: homeowner
works: The old hands at the yard take {N} in as one of their own, and stand by {N} from the first week.
works: Within a month the crew knows {Ns} name and {Ns} family's, and they cover for each other without being asked.
fails: After the long months out of work, the yard's pay will not stretch to the mortgage, and by winter the house is sold.
fails: The arrears grow a little every month on the yard's wage, and in the end the bank takes the house.

