fails: {N} keeps away from the hall, and the gap grows.

== bold: the supper that ran short / R
base: skip the supper, and throw a party in the barn for your friends
likelier_if: has [dancing] +10; has [name on the local scene] +5
- R | throw a barn dance for the whole town at your own cost, and invite everyone | v: hedonism, benevolence | act: throw a barn dance for the whole town at their own cost | chance: 30 | requires: savings | grants: name on the local scene | takes_if_fails: savings
works: Half the town comes to the barn, and from then on {N} is a name everyone knows at every party.
works: The dance runs till dawn, and {Ns} name is back on everyone's lips, kindly this time.
fails: Hardly anyone comes, and the band and the food take every penny saved.
fails: It rains, the barn leaks, the crowd goes home early, and the night costs all {Ns} savings.

== bold: a bumper harvest / B
base: buy grain cheap now and store it to sell in the spring
likelier_if: has [farmer] +10; has [selling] +5
- B | borrow to buy up the valley's surplus, and sell it all in the city in spring | v: power, achievement | act: borrow to buy up the valley's surplus and sell it all in the city in spring | chance: 30 | grants: striking a deal | title_if_fails: bankruptcy or insolvency in their history
works: Spring comes, the city buyers pay twice the autumn price, and from then on {N} knows how to drive a bargain.
works: {N} haggles every load into the best price of the year, and has a dealer's nose for good.
fails: Prices stay low into the spring, half the stock spoils, the loans cannot be paid, and {N} goes through a formal insolvency.
fails: The city market is as flooded as the valley, the bank calls the loans in, and {N} is declared insolvent.
